TI  - ThermiQuant AquaStream: A portable instrument for quantitative colorimetric 
      isothermal nucleic acid amplification reactions in paper and tube formats.
PG  - e0348607
LID - 10.1371/journal.pone.0348607 [doi]
LID - e0348607
AB  - Microfluidic paper-based analytical devices (microPADs) are an attractive format for 
      colorimetric nucleic acid amplification tests (NAATs) because they enable 
      low-cost, portable diagnostics in resource-limited settings. However, researchers 
      often optimize colorimetric assays in liquid reactions in tubes before 
      translating them to microPADs. Since both formats require separate instruments for 
      incubation and real-time sensing, direct comparison of reactions between the two 
      formats is difficult. To address these cross-platform limitations, we developed 
      ThermiQuant AquaStream, a portable benchtop device (15 x 20 x 16 cm, ~ 5 kg; 
      cost: USD 327) that supports seamless colorimetric loop-mediated isothermal 
      amplification (LAMP) reactions in both microPADs and tubes under a common workflow. 
      The system enables real-time reaction tracking (every 30 seconds) through onboard 
      image processing, precise isothermal control (+/-0.5  degrees C) using a repurposed 
      consumer-grade sous-vide heater, and medium-throughput (24 tubes or 42 microPADs). 
      Testing with synthetic SARS-CoV-2 orf7ab DNA fragments demonstrated a limit of 
      detection corresponding to a 95% probability of detection (LOD95) of 110 copies 
      per reaction in tube (22 copies/microL) and 39 copies per reaction in microPADs (5 
      copies/microL), estimated using probit regression. In both formats the limit of 
      quantification (LOQ), defined as the lowest concentration yielding a coefficient 
      of variation (CV) of quantification time (Tq) </= 10%, was 250 copies/reaction 
      resulting in a strong linear (R2 = 0.98 & R2 = 0.96 respectively for tube and 
      microPADs) standard calibration curves. ThermiQuant AquaStream provides an 
      affordable and versatile benchtop platform capable of supporting both tube- and 
      microPAD-based colorimetric LAMP assays, serving as a proof-of-concept research tool 
      for assay development and molecular diagnostics in One Health settings such as 
      clinics, farms, and field environments.
