TI  - 3-mercaptopropionic acid agent-based biosensor system using gold-screen printed 
      electrode for aflatoxin B1 detection.
PG  - 117411
LID - S0731-7085(26)00079-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jpba.2026.117411 [doi]
AB  - A novel electrochemical biosensor was constructed for the ultrasensitive 
      detection of aflatoxin B1 (AFB1) in food samples. The biosensor design was based 
      on a 3-mercaptopropionic acid (3-MPA)-modified self-assembled monolayer (SAM) 
      constructed on disposable gold screen-printed electrodes (SPE-Au). Covalent 
      attachment of anti-AFB1 antibodies was achieved on the functionalized electrode 
      surface, and the modification process at each stage was analyzed using CV and EIS 
      techniques. 3-MPA concentration was optimized to enhance analytical performance. 
      The biosensor exhibited a wide linear detection range of 0.1-250 pg/mL with a 
      calculated limit of detection (LOD) of 0.94 pg/mL and limit of quantification 
      (LOQ) of 3.14 pg/mL. It also demonstrated high reproducibility and excellent 
      selectivity toward AFB1. Finally, the biosensor was successfully applied to real 
      food samples, including milk, rice, peanuts, and chili pepper, confirming its 
      reliability and potential for practical food safety monitoring.
