TI  - Integrated lab-in-syringe/lab-on-valve flow system for the synthesis of 
      EDTA-capped silver nanoparticles and determination of creatinine.
PG  - 128853
LID - S0039-9140(25)01344-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.talanta.2025.128853 [doi]
AB  - A fully integrated lab-in-syringe/lab-on-valve flow system was developed for the 
      synthesis of EDTA-capped silver nanoparticles and their subsequent application in 
      the spectrophotometric determination of creatinine. This work presents the first 
      use of a lab-in-syringe system for nanoparticle synthesis and the first fully 
      integrated flow system that unites both synthesis and analysis steps within a 
      single system. The method is based on the aggregation of silver nanoparticles 
      induced by creatinine in an alkaline medium, with detection performed by 
      spectrophotometric measurement of the resulting colour change. The method was 
      successfully applied to the determination of creatinine in human serum samples. 
      Analytical validation of the method confirmed a limit of detection (LOD) of 
      0.04 mg/L and a limit of quantification (LOQ) of 0.14 mg/L. A linear range 
      between 0.14 and 3.00 mg/L was obtained, with a relative error (RE) of 6.7 % and 
      a coefficient of variation (CV, n=8) of 8.0 %, confirming satisfactory accuracy.
